{"units": [{"id": "eimi_sum-note10", "translation": "The present indicative εἰμί [I am] is found at Pr. 14, 509. Sept. 41, 808. Pers. 1036. Ag. 104, 757, 1195. Ch. 219, 674, 1026. Eum. 445, 455, 712. Suppl. 250. | εἶ [you are] at Pr. 696. Sept. 977, 989. Ag. 1105, 1140, 1360, 1421, 1426, 1505. Eum. 722, 847. Suppl. 202. Fr. 67, 275, 4. ἐστί [he/she/it is] at Pr. 50, 105, 107, 197, 515, 517, 521, 753, 755, 842, 954. Sept. 224, 367, 413, 447, 599, 625, [649.] Pers. 165, 210, 347, 349, 513, 688, 693, 1033. Ag. 160, 259, 272, 428, 478, 832, 1232, 1404, 1487, 1561. Ch. 115, 122, 170, 422, 514, 519, 656, 673, 703, 710, 733. Eum. 19, 62, 244, 272, 350, 480, 576, 658, 692, 753, 885. Suppl. 82, 188, 320, 440, 514, 741, 824, 959, 1047, 1048. Fr. 19, 41, 7, 173, 175, 179, 196, 5, 226, 232, 257, 278, 241, 288, 296, 307, 395. ἐστόν [you two are] at Ch. 207. ἐσμέν [we are] at [Sept. 516.] Eum. 416, 585, 774. ἐστέ [you (plural) are] at Eum. 408, 824. Suppl. 280. εἰσί [they are] at Pr. 378. Sept. 940. Pers. 690, 869. Eum. 118. ὦ [I may be] at Pers. 692. Eum. 678. ἢ [you may be] at Pers. 791. Ch 177. εἴην [I would be] at Sept. 188. Ag. 472. εἴης [you would be] at Pr. 979. εἴη [he/she/it would be] at Pr. 494. Sept. 670. Ag. 216. Ch. 868. Eum. 1012. Suppl. 356, 488, 1055. εἶεν [they would be] at Suppl. 185. Imperative ἴσθι [be!] at Sept. 238. Ag. 512. Ch. 147. Eum. 91. ἔστω [let him/her/it be] at Ag. 378. Eum. 549, 864. Suppl. 664, 687. ἔστε [be! (plural)] at Sept. 180. Ch. 98 in both places ἐστέ is written, which is the accent of the indicative, not the imperative: on which there is an explicit rule of Herodian vol. 1 p. 465, 2. and vol. 2 p. 41, 11 ed. Lentz. || ὤν [being] at Pr. 62, 594. Sept. 605, 1010. Pers. 224, 749, 782, 1039. Ag. 988, 1352, 1585, 1608, 1619. Ch. 199, 866. Eum. 90, 153, 176, 297, 356, 551, 615. Suppl. 371, 617, 914. Fr. 391. ὄντι [to the one being] at Pr. 308. ὄντα [being (acc.)] at Pr. 983. Sept. 1015. Pers. 820. Ag. 464, 1605, 1606. Ch. 224. Eum. 358, 413, 475. Ag. 650. ὄντας [being (acc. pl.)] at Pr. 443. Pers. 175. Ch. 234. ὄντα [being (neut. pl.)] at Pr. 499. Ag. 1571. Suppl. 55. οὖσα [being (fem.)] at Sept. 201, 265, 1034. Pers. 162. Ag. 593, 1048. Ch. 196, 758. Eum. 733. || εἶναι [to be] at Pr. 217, 314, 386, 686, 737, 741. Sept. 266, 411, 592, 646, 1024. Pers. 627. Ag. 788, 840, 1037, 1094, 1131, 1375, 1497, 1499. Ch. 193, 541, 874, 1032. Eum. 312, 425, 448, 891. Suppl. 389, 454, 536, 614, 761, 917."}, {"id": "eimi_sum-note11", "translation": "The first person of the imperfect ἢ [I was] at Ag. 1637, about which we spoke above p. 103. Second person ῆσθα [you were] at Ag. 1211. Ch. 243. Third person ἣν [he/she/it was] at Pr. 754 [887.] Sept. 491, 675, 812, 1050. Pers. 334, 338, 340, 350, 371, 407, 720, 765, 777, 957. Ag. 168, 842, 1205, 1395, 1396, 1460, 1636. Ch. 177, 197, 198, 360 (where now ἦν [he/she/it was]), 532, 699, 704. Suppl. 244, 245, 343. Fr. 259. ἔσκε [he/she/it was] at Pers. 656. ἦτε [you (plural) were] at Ag. 542. Suppl. 288. Plural ἦσαν [they were] at Pr. 674. Pers. 343, 398, 423, 441. Ag. 859. Ch. 975. Suppl. 565."}]}